{
  "_doc": "LN1 line types (src/lines.h, docs/lines.md). A line is an Instance of `asset` (content/assets/line_<id>.json, a \"line\" block naming this type) with its points in extra.line. `builder` names a LINE_BUILDER (\"trench\": the GX1 trench network in terrain_blend.cpp). `spacing`: nominal bay length (m); `params`: per-type defaults a line may override. LN2 appends fence, wire, wall and hedge types here. LN2 types (builder \"bays\", src/lines_ln2.cpp): `pieces` [[asset id, weight]] laid as bays along the line (stretched to fit); `sectionHp`: each bay is a damage section (wire / sandbags: a blast cuts it out); `hedge`: nav marks the banks as walls; `gates`: gate pieces that join the type's chains in migration and the gate kinds its spans take; `minChain`: fewest joined pieces migrated (single knife rests stay obstacles); `migrate`: pieces turned into this type on map load (also hidden from the Assets palette), with an optional asset-space `path` and a `gap` [s0, s1] (a gateway inside the piece). Spans: {s: centre arc length, w: width, kind: gap | field_gate | gate_piers}.",
